
<p>David Pogue, at Pogue’s Posts:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>Amazon’s “50+ things to try” list mentions that Alexa can “find a
home maintenance professional.” So I tried it.</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>ME: I need a septic-system repair.</p>

<p>ALEXA: That service isn’t currently supported. I can help with
plumbing services instead.</p>

<p>ME: Okay, fine. Plumbing services.</p>

<p>ALEXA: What’s your plumbing issue?</p>

<p>ME: I have untreated sewage pouring out of my kitchen faucet.</p>

<p>ALEXA: Is this urgent?</p>

<p><em>Uh … what do YOU think, dumbass? But OK:</em></p>

<p>ME: Yes.</p>

<p>ALEXA: When do you need it by?</p>

<p><em>Displays four responses: <strong>ASAP</strong>, <strong>Within a week</strong>, <strong>Further
out</strong>, and <strong>I haven’t decided yet</strong>.</em></p>

<p>ME: ASAP.</p>

<p>ALEXA: I’m Alexa, not Shaq.</p>
</blockquote>
</blockquote>

<p>This could only have been funnier if Alexa had responded “The Aristocrats!”</p>

<p>(Which great film, is, in fact, <a href="https://www.amazon.com/Aristocrats-Jason-Alexander/dp/B07VQNWBLT">available to stream on Amazon Prime</a>.)</p>

